MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Carole King and Bread feel like natural next choices because their warm vocals and gentle melodies connect with what I enjoy in Simon & Garfunkel and Melanie.",
    "The Beach Boys match my interest in Beatles-era songs and AM Gold, while Neil Diamond offers the melodic songwriting and familiar hits I am looking for."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Adele's albums do not fit my current wish to revisit older folk-pop and familiar sixties songs, even though emotional singing can appeal to me.",
    "Bowie's theatrical rock feels farther from today's mood; Queen and Elvis have some appeal, but I would choose the gentler selections first."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in classic rock seems to have been taken as equal interest in very different sounds, when warmth and gentleness matter more to me today.",
    "A greatest-hits title helps, but that format alone does not make an artist feel as close a match as Bread, Neil Diamond, or the Beach Boys."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My listening to Melanie, Simon & Garfunkel, and Jonathan Edwards points toward intimate songwriting and acoustic warmth that I want more of now.",
    "Although I have listened to Born This Way, that does not mean contemporary pop is my priority on this visit; my repeated interest in older songs better reflects today's choices."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in older favorites, but sometimes miss that gentle melodies, harmonies, and warm songwriting are what draw me in today."
}
